# `actions/checkout` on the Windows runners uses git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which would hand the eight `.snap` files under
# crates/heyl-domain/tests/snapshots/ CRLF endings and fail every `insta`
# comparison for a reason that has nothing to do with the code. Normalising the
# whole tree is the fix that also covers tests/fixtures/protocol/ and whatever
# textual fixture is added next.
#
# `descriptors/heylogin.binpb` and the other binary artifacts are detected as
# binary by `text=auto` and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
